## Install

LiteArm Studio ships as one self-contained program: no Python, no Node.js and no repository
checkout.

* Ubuntu and Debian: `litearm-studio-{{version}}_amd64.deb` — `sudo apt install ./litearm-studio-{{version}}_amd64.deb`
* Other Linux: `litearm-studio-{{version}}-linux-amd64` — verify the `.sha256`, `chmod +x` it, then run it.
* Windows: `litearm-studio-{{version}}-windows-amd64.exe` — verify the `.sha256`, then double-click it.

Ubuntu 22.04 / Debian 12 or newer is required (glibc 2.35). Serial-port access, the gripper and
first-run activation are covered in [docs/INSTALL.md]({{@root.host}}/{{@root.owner}}/{{@root.repository}}/blob/{{currentTag}}/docs/INSTALL.md).
